lib/kroki-include-line-filters.js adapts that package's own
lib/include/include-processor.js (its lines=/tag=/tags= include-selection
functions, `getLines`/`filterLinesByLineNumbers`/`getTags`/
`filterLinesByTags`) to operate on plain JS strings and objects instead of
Opal/Asciidoctor's Reader and Hash — needed so kroki-prewarm.js can filter a
diagram's include::-resolved source the same way real Asciidoctor conversion
would, before Asciidoctor itself has run (see that file's own header for
why). Per MPL-2.0 §1.10(a), a Modification of Covered Software remains
MPL-2.0 regardless of how much of it has changed — see that file's own
header for exactly what was adapted.

Every other file in this package — including kroki-prewarm.js itself, which
only calls the upstream package's own public API
(@antora/asciidoc-loader/include/resolve-include-file) as a normal npm
dependency rather than copying from it — is wholly Inditex's own work and
